
# <type>[optional scope][!]: <description>
#
# [optional body]
#
# [optional footer(s)]
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits 1.0.0 — https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
#
# Types (enforced by commitlint, see commitlint.config.mjs):
#   feat      A new feature                         -> MINOR bump
#   fix       A bug fix                             -> PATCH bump
#   docs      Documentation only
#   style     Formatting, no code change
#   refactor  Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf      Performance improvement
#   test      Adding or correcting tests
#   build     Build system, dependencies, packaging
#   ci        CI configuration and workflows
#   chore     Maintenance that does not touch src/ or test/
#   revert    Reverts a previous commit
#
# Breaking changes: add "!" after type/scope AND/OR a footer
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>                  -> MAJOR bump
#
# Rules:
#   - Description: imperative mood, lower case, no trailing period, <= 100 chars header.
#   - Body: explain *what* and *why*, wrapped at 100 columns.
#   - Footers: "Refs: #123", "Closes: #123", "BREAKING CHANGE: ...".
#
# Enable this template locally with:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
